@startuml
title Kids Flashcards - package architecture
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Visitor / child" as Visitor
actor "Series owner" as Owner
package "Angular SPA (src/frontend)" {
  [Interface language (English / French)] as Language
  [Browser localStorage preference] as Preference
  [Login / callback / logout] as Login
  [Edit Mode] as Edit
  [Practice Mode] as Practice
  [Angular Location / browser history] as Navigation
  [CSS 3D card faces] as Faces
  [REST API client] as Client
  [Bootstrap / Font Awesome] as Styles
  [toastr notifications] as Toast
}
package "Python API (src/backend)" {
  [FastAPI REST routes] as Routes
  [Life2 exchange proxy] as Exchange
  [JWT verification / HttpOnly session] as Auth
  [Visibility / immutable ownership policy] as Access
  [Request validation] as Validation
  [SQLAlchemy persistence] as Persistence
  [Protected picture upload / serving] as Uploads
  [Explicit auth schema migration] as Migration
}
package "Existing Life2 services" {
  [Auth registered application sign-in] as Life2
  [One-time origin-bound handoff exchange] as Handoff
}
database "PostgreSQL on localhost\nkids_flashcards" as Database
folder "Local persisted uploads\ndata/uploads" as Files
file "Life2 signing-key file\nserver-only configuration" as Key

Visitor --> Practice : public series
Owner --> Practice : public + own private series
Owner --> Edit : manage own series / cards / visibility
Visitor --> Login : header login button
Login --> Life2 : applicationId + exact callback URL
Life2 --> Login : /auth/callback?handoff_code=...
Login --> Client : scrub code; exchange then establish session
Client --> Exchange : same-origin POST /api/auth/exchange
Exchange --> Handoff : fixed Auth URL; allowed Origin
Handoff --> Exchange : Life2 account JWT
Client --> Auth : POST /api/auth/session
Auth --> Key : verify HS256 signature
Routes --> Auth : validate cookie / bearer claims
Routes --> Access : visible series / owner-only mutation
Access --> Persistence : subject + account matching
Auth --> Client : HttpOnly SameSite=Lax cookie
Owner --> Navigation : deep links / Back / Forward
Edit --> Navigation : /set/<UUID>/edit
Practice --> Navigation : /set/<UUID>/practice
Navigation --> Client : restore visible set from path
Visitor --> Language : header flag switch
Language --> Preference : remember en / fr only
Edit ..> Language : labels / notifications
Practice ..> Language : accessibility / labels
Edit --> Client
Practice --> Client : load visible set
Practice --> Faces : rotate on click / Space
Edit ..> Styles
Practice ..> Styles
Edit ..> Toast : success / failure feedback
Login ..> Toast : authentication results
Client --> Routes : same-origin JSON / multipart
Routes --> Validation
Routes --> Persistence
Routes --> Uploads
Uploads --> Access : referenced visible series or upload owner
Uploads --> Persistence : upload ownership metadata
Persistence --> Database
Migration --> Database : explicit additive schema change
Uploads --> Files
Practice --> Uploads : protected HTTP pictures
Edit --> Uploads : owned upload previews

note bottom of Auth
  Validate algorithm, signature, issuer, audience, exp, iat,
  subject, accountId, and registered applicationId.
  Cookie writes require an allowed Origin.
  No tokens or handoff codes in browser storage.
end note
note bottom of Access
  Public: anyone may read / practise; only owner may edit.
  Private: only matching subject and account may read / edit.
  New series are private; ownership is assigned server-side.
  All mutations and uploads require authentication.
  Inaccessible series / pictures return 404.
end note
note bottom of Practice
  Library / sidebar links open Practice.
  Only owners can restore Edit via a direct link.
  Shuffled order persists for previous / next.
  Navigation / reshuffle resets to the front.
end note
note bottom of Faces
  Grid faces preserve height; backfaces are hidden.
  400 ms rotateY; instant with reduced motion.
  Only the active face is exposed to assistive technology.
end note
note bottom of Language
  French by default; flags select French / English.
  Practice state, drafts, and stored content are unchanged.
  No API or database language setting.
end note
@enduml
